.ccv4-root{
    --ink:#0E0E10;
    --muted:#6B6B72;
    --line:#E6E4E0;
    --line-2:#ECEDEF;
    --bg-2:#F2F3F5;
    --violet:#8E4DFF;
    font-family:var(--font-body-family,'Helvetica Neue',Inter,system-ui,sans-serif);
    color:var(--ink);
    padding:40px 0 48px;
    background:#fff;
  }
  .ccv4{max-width:1440px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px}
  @media(max-width:720px){.ccv4{padding:0 20px}.ccv4-root{padding:40px 0}}

  .ccv4-head{margin-bottom:28px;text-align:center}
  .ccv4-eyebrow{font-family:var(--font-mono-family,ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);display:block;margin-bottom:8px}
  .ccv4-h2{font-size:clamp(26px,2.6vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.05;margin:0 0 10px;font-weight:600}
  .ccv4-sub{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 auto;max-width:56ch;line-height:1.5}

  /* Desktop grid */
  .ccv4-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:140px repeat(var(--cols), minmax(0, 1fr));
    border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:16px;
    overflow:hidden;
    background:#fff;
  }
  .ccv4-row{display:contents}
  .ccv4-cell{padding:18px 14px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2);background:#fff}
  .ccv4-cell--label{font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);justify-content:flex-start;text-align:left;border-right:1px solid var(--line-2);flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:2px}
  .ccv4-cell--label .row-sub{font-family:var(--font-mono-family,ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);font-weight:400}
  .ccv4-cell--spacer{background:#fff;border-right:1px solid var(--line-2);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2)}
  .ccv4-row--alt .ccv4-cell{background:var(--bg-2)}
  .ccv4-row:last-of-type .ccv4-cell{border-bottom:none}

  .ccv4-row--head .ccv4-cell--photo{flex-direction:column;gap:6px;padding:20px 12px 14px;background:#fff;justify-content:flex-end}
  .ccv4-photo-link{text-decoration:none;color:inherit;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:8px}
  /* Fixed frame, image pinned to the floor: the cases line up on one baseline so the
     height difference between them is the real height difference. Width is left to the
     intrinsic ratio - constraining it would undo the scale. */
  /* NO max-width HERE. The renders are square 900x900 canvases, so an image set to 216px
     tall is also 216px wide - wider than the 165px column - and max-width:100% then
     crushed it back down, which silently undid the scale: H7 Flow, the TALLEST case, drew
     smallest. photo_max_px must stay at or under the usable column width instead. */
  .ccv4-photo-frame{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;width:100%;overflow:visible}
  .ccv4-photo-link img{width:auto;max-width:none;height:auto;object-fit:contain}
  .ccv4-name{font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin:6px 0 0;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .ccv4-note{margin:14px 2px 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted)}
  .ccv4-tiers{font-size:12px;margin-top:2px;color:var(--muted)}
  .ccv4-tiers a{color:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px}
  .ccv4-tiers a:hover{color:var(--violet)}
  .ccv4-tiers .sep{color:rgba(14,14,16,.25);margin:0 4px}

  /* List-style cells (Fan / Radiator support) */
  .ccv4-cell--list{text-align:left;justify-content:flex-start;padding:16px 12px}
  /* Label ABOVE value, not beside it. Side by side, the label ate half a 200px column and
     "3 x 120 / 3 x 140 mm" broke mid-number across four lines. Stacked, the value gets the
     full width and stays on one or two clean lines. */
  .ccv4-cell--list .cell-inner{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;width:100%;min-width:0}
  .ccv4-cell--list .kv{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px;min-width:0}
  .ccv4-cell--list .k{
    font-family:var(--font-mono-family,ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace);
    font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;
    font-weight:500;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;
  }
  .ccv4-cell--list .v{font-weight:500;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:normal;word-break:keep-all}

  /* Mobile: keep the grid visible, make it side-scrollable */
  .ccv4-mobile{display:none}
  @media(max-width:1023px){
    .ccv4-grid{
      grid-template-columns:130px repeat(var(--cols), 200px);
      overflow-x:auto;
      overflow-y:hidden;
      scroll-snap-type:x proximity;
      scrollbar-width:none;
      -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;
      border-radius:12px;
    }
    .ccv4-grid::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
    .ccv4-cell{padding:14px 10px;font-size:13px}
    .ccv4-cell--list{padding:12px 10px}
    .ccv4-cell--list .k{font-size:9px}
    .ccv4-cell--list .v{font-size:12px}
    .ccv4-row--head .ccv4-cell--photo{padding:14px 8px 12px;scroll-snap-align:start}
    .ccv4-photo-link img{max-width:none}
    .ccv4-name{font-size:15px}
    .ccv4-mobile{display:none}
    .ccv4-card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:20px;background:#fff}
    .ccv4-card__main{text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block}
    .ccv4-card__head{display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:14px}
    .ccv4-card__img{width:84px;height:84px;object-fit:contain;flex-shrink:0}
    .ccv4-card__name{font-size:18px;font-weight:600;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.01em}
    .ccv4-card__dim{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin:4px 0 0;font-family:var(--font-mono-family,ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace);letter-spacing:.08em}
    .ccv4-card__specs{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line-2)}
    .ccv4-card__spec{display:grid;grid-template-columns:120px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline}
    .ccv4-card__spec .k{font-family:var(--font-mono-family,ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);font-weight:500;padding-top:2px}
    .ccv4-card__spec .v{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--ink);font-weight:500}
    .ccv4-card__tiers{margin-top:14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line-2);font-size:13px}
    .ccv4-card__tiers a{color:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px}
    .ccv4-card__tiers .sep{color:rgba(14,14,16,.25);margin:0 6px}
  }
Frequently Asked Questions
How much PSU wattage do I need?
Add up the power draw of your CPU and graphics card, add about 100 W for the rest of the system, then leave 20–30% headroom. Most mid-range gaming builds land at 750–850 W. High-end graphics cards often call for 1,000 W or more, so check the maker's recommended PSU wattage for your card.
What does ATX 3.1 mean on a power supply?
ATX 3.1 is Intel's current power supply standard. ATX 3.1 units handle the short power spikes that modern graphics cards create, and they use the 12V-2x6 connector for high-power cards. The C850 Gold Core, for example, is ATX 3.1 with a 600 W 12V-2x6 cable.
What do 80 PLUS Bronze, Gold and Platinum mean?
80 PLUS ratings measure how efficiently a power supply turns wall power into power your PC can use. Higher tiers waste less energy as heat. On 115 V, Gold units must be at least 87% efficient at 20% load, 90% at 50% and 87% at 100%. Platinum raises the bar to 90%, 92% and 89%.
What is a fully modular power supply?
With a fully modular PSU, every cable detaches, including the 24-pin motherboard cable. You connect only the cables your build needs, which cuts clutter and makes cable management and future upgrades easier. Gold Core power supplies such as the C850 Gold Core are fully modular.
Is a quiet power supply worth it?
If you care about noise, yes. Many PSUs have a zero-RPM fan mode that stops the fan at low loads, so the PSU is silent while you browse or work. The C850 Gold Core has a zero-RPM mode and a Cybenetics A++ noise rating.
